;; (HELP defun)
macro (defun name formals &rest expr)
  Defines a named function in the current package.
  Malformed lambda lists and duplicate parameter names are errors at
  creation; see lambda for parameter-list and duplicate keyword rules.
  The lisp package is sealed after initialization; defining a name there
  signals:
  cannot rebind lisp package binding: name. Unqualified builtin
  shadowing in your own package remains legal.
=> ()
;; (HELP let)
operator (let bindings &rest expr)
  Creates local variable bindings evaluated in parallel. All value
  expressions are evaluated in the enclosing scope before any
  bindings are established. The first argument is a list of
  [symbol value] pairs. Duplicate names are legal (the last binding wins),
  but lint warns; use let* for sequential rebinding. Returns the last body
  value.
=> ()
